 # Neural Transient Field (NeTF)
-
-
 ## Overview
-NeTF is a neural modeling framework for Non-Line-of-Sight (NLOS) imaging that recovers the 5D transient function (spatial location and direction) implicitly represented by a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) [S1]. Unlike NeRF, which parametrizes input training data along lines (rays), NeTF parametrizes input training data on spherical wavefronts [S1]. It addresses the challenge of sparse and unbalanced sampling in NLOS by using Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) and a two-stage training strategy [S1].
-
